Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Derive the ladder by scanning the artifacts instead of
 pinning it

report_data documented itself as hardcoding one thing: the list of timestamps each arm is
read from. That was the last place where a new artifact could be ignored, and the only list
in the pipeline nobody could re-check on screen.

scan() walks every launch directory under outputs/, including the six that died before
writing a scored run, and records status, error-turn count and both statistics for each.
discover() then takes the newest complete, scored, zero-error artifact per arm -- the rule
the two offline harnesses already use, so the report and the analyses can no longer drift
onto different episodes -- and raises if an arm has nothing usable at all. The timestamps
the sprint analysed stay in the file as recorded provenance, and selection() reports drift
against them rather than being governed by them.

On today's tree the scan chooses the same seven artifacts it replaced, and its accounting
closes: 19 launches, 11 usable, 7 chosen, 4 superseded, 1 rejected for error turns, 1 scored
but incomplete, 6 that never wrote a run. Running the module prints that table first, so the
selection is visible instead of asserted.
